  "title": "Enhanced Feedback & Tool Visibility Controls",
  "summary": "Discovery Engine now offers more granular feedback options, including specific reasons for positive responses and a dedicated structure for disputing Model Armor verdicts. New schemas also hint at future fine-grained control over tool visibility.",
  "details": "Developers can now provide richer positive feedback on search results or generated content using new enum values in `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaFeedback.reasons`: `RELEVANT`, `COMPREHENSIVE`, `GOOD_CITATION`, and `ACCURATE`. A new optional field, `modelArmorDisputeInfo`, has been added to `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaFeedback`. This field, backed by the new `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaFeedbackModelArmorDisputeInfo` schema, allows users to submit detailed information when disputing Model Armor's `BLOCK` or `FLAG` verdicts, including `expectedLabel`, `sanitizationResultJson`, and `templateName`. This is crucial for refining AI safety models. Additionally, new schemas `ApiservingMcpMcpToolVisibility` and `ApiservingMcpMcpToolVisibilityFieldVisibility` have been introduced, laying groundwork for defining and enforcing visibility restrictions on 'MCP tools' and their fields, though the `visibilityEnforcementStrategy` is explicitly marked as 'DO NOT USE' for now. Finally, `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1betaProvisionProjectRequest` now includes an optional `idpConfig` field, enabling the specification of an Identity Provider configuration during project provisioning to streamline AclConfig setup.",
